# fctry .fctry/ track-vs-ignore policy — CANONICAL SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# This file is the single declared contract for which .fctry/ paths git
# TRACKS (durable source-of-truth) and which it IGNORES (ephemeral). It is
# copied verbatim into a project's .fctry/.gitignore at init
# (scripts/init-agent-model.sh) and create-OR-reconciled on every prompt by the
# migrate hook (hooks/migrate.sh — create_gitignore when absent, gitignore-policy.js
# reconcileGitignore when present-but-stale; cycle 131 / GH #249). The reader, the
# canonical-pattern lists, the drift check, and the reconcile writer live in
# src/process/gitignore-policy.js; doctor
# Check 46 (scripts/verify-gitignore-policy.sh) verifies a project's
# .fctry/.gitignore against this contract. Mirrors how cycle 90 / GH #138
# lifted the phase model into src/process/default-process.json +
# src/process/load.js (cycle 115 / GH #140, subsumes #191).
#
# ── TRACKED (canonical durable source-of-truth) ──────────────────────────
# Git tracks these .fctry/ paths; they are the operational state every
# session reads against and reconciles. Do NOT add ignore lines for them.
#   config.json              version registry + format version
#   lessons.md               cross-session learnings (candidate → active)
#   process.json             declared phase model (cycle 90 / GH #138)
#   routing.json             declared model-routing policy (cycle 124 / GH #172 #173)
#   audits/                  conformance audits
#   cycles/<N>/{diagnose,scope,build,close}.md   phase artifacts
#   refs/<UTC>-<slug>.json   research_verdict artifacts (/fctry:ref)
#   steward.json             /close steward marker + sha-chain
#   harvest-watermark.json   cross-repo harvest cursor (durable — loss forces
#                            a full re-scan; body-marker dedupe keeps it safe
#                            but not free; see scripts/harvest-fctry-core.sh)
#   launchd/com.fctry.harvest.plist   in-repo LaunchAgent source-of-truth
#   m4-pro/                  m4-pro worker scripts (install-m4-pro-*.sh deploys)
#   agent-model-init         init-agent-model.sh sentinel
#   substrate-tier           init-substrate.sh sentinel
#   legacy-spec-era/         migration archive of legacy spec-era files
#   no-session-handoff, no-statusline, no-orchestrator-edit-guard,
#     no-summary-surface, no-stuck-loop, and any future no-* opt-out sentinels
#   .gitignore               this file itself
#
# ── LEGACY / project-shape (tracked when present; migration-era) ─────────
# Carried for projects mid-migration; not written fresh by fctry-next.
#   spec.db, architecture.md, viewer/, doom-loop-state.json,
#   build-trace-*.md, interview-state.md
#
# ── IGNORED (always ephemeral) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The lines below are the ignore body. Project-specific additions are
# allowed beneath the canonical block: doctor Check 46 passes silently on
# additions, WARNS on a missing canonical entry (drift), and FAILS on a
# missing canonical-REQUIRED body entry OR a missing TRACKED-file entry in
# the header block above (cycle 128 / GH #256). The required/recommended
# split lives in src/process/gitignore-policy.js, not in this file's comments.
#
# When this set GROWS, existing adopters self-heal: hooks/migrate.sh reconciles
# a present-but-stale .fctry/.gitignore on the next prompt (append the new
# patterns, refresh a drifted header) via gitignore-policy.js reconcileGitignore
# — no hand-editing (cycle 131 / GH #249). So adding a line here propagates to
# every adopter automatically; you don't have to touch their copies.

# --- canonical-required (must be ignored; doctor fails if missing) ---
state.json
inbox.json
session-handoff.md
.context-state.json
sessions/
coordination/
.migration-policy.json
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# --- canonical-recommended (doctor warns if missing) ---
tool-check
plugin-root
resume-index.json
pre-compact-snapshot.json
quality-baseline.json
# canonical loop-state projection (src/process/loop-state.js, GH #282) — derived view
loop-state.json
# stuck-loop detector's session-runtime ring buffer (hooks/stuck-loop-detect.js, GH #228)
stuck-state.json
.cache/
autonomous
cycles/*/fixtures/proj/
wave/
.summary-surfaced
.summary-surface-challenge
# per-cycle fire-once diagnose-hook sentinels (.diagnose-{inbox-drain,km-pulse,km-search}-fired-<N>)
.diagnose-*-fired-*
.DS_Store
